{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSPasswordInput","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/Controls"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Layout","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Layout"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Passwords input is based on several configurable UI elements:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"label","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": It is used to describe the purpose of the input.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"placeholder"}]},{"text":":  A prefix is not common and is discouraged in a Password Input component. In very specific cases, it can provide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context or format requirements (e.g., “DEV-” for test accounts, “admin-” as a pattern to define an admin password)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"lock icon","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": it helps to reinforce the security context."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Helper text","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":":  A supporting text conveys additional information about the password field.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Outlined style","anchor":"Outlined-style"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"default"}]},{"type":"text","text":", the input is with a subtle background fill and invisible bottom border, creating a softer and more contained look."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["   \/\/ An outlined text input","   OUDSPasswordInput(label: \"Your password\", password: $password, isOutlined: true)","","   \/\/ With a localizable from a bundle","   OUDSPasswordInput(LocalizedStringKey(\"password_label\"), bundle: Bundle.module, password: $password)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Rounded layout","anchor":"Rounded-layout","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As the"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":" OUDSTextInput"},{"type":"text","text":", rounded corners can be enabled or disabled using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasRoundedTextInputs"},{"type":"text","text":" values of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tuning"},{"text":" object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"in your theme configuration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Status","anchor":"Status","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSPasswordInput","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is based on the","type":"text"},{"code":" OUDSTextInput","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", all the status are the same and have the same behavior available here ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSTextInput.Status","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"anchor":"Accessibility-considerations","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Accessibility considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By default no haptics are done by the component for the trailing action.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However you should think about cases wher you will have to make the devices vibrates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"You can refer to the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/design\/human-interface-guidelines\/playing-haptics"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Rich text","anchor":"Rich-text","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rich text can be used for error and helper texts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strong text can be used sparingly to highlight key information within the content.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"No other text styles should be used."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Underlined text must not be applied manually (e.g. in error message), as it is commonly associated with hyperlinks and may mislead users."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Code-samples","type":"heading","text":"Code samples"},{"code":["    \/\/ The password to display and edit","    @State var password: String = \"\"","","    \/\/ A basic password input with label","    OUDSPasswordInput(label: \"Password\", password: $password)","","    \/\/ Add a leading icon and helper text to more context","    OUDSPasswordInput(label: \"Password\", password: $password, lockIcon: true, helperText: \"Your password must be between 8 and 20 characters long.\")","","    \/\/ Password with prefix","    OUDSPasswordInput(label: \"Password\", password: $password, prefix: \"CORP-\")","","    \/\/ Make password visible","    OUDSPasswordInput(label: \"Password\", password: $password, isHiddenPassword: .constant(false))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Design-documentation","type":"heading","text":"Design documentation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-password-input"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Themes rendering","type":"heading","anchor":"Themes-rendering"},{"level":3,"text":"Orange","type":"heading","anchor":"Orange"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_passwordInput_Orange","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Orange Compact","type":"heading","anchor":"Orange-Compact"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"i